                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "12429861",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198083205225",
                            "num_reviews": 5,
                            "playtime_forever": 58,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 58,
                            "last_played": 1412901041
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I found this to be a lot of fun. It is the same kind of light repetitive difficult fun as Super Meat Boy, for example. But it does allow you to save your progress and give you infinite lives, which I really like. The story is simple, with nice characters, and the art (especially the planets and game menus!) and soundtrack are pretty awesome.\nThe direction controls are a little strange, particularly moving from a planet to another, because of the difference in their gravities. It takes a few tries to get used to them, but you eventually do. Also, I've been told the developers are working on an update to improve this. (I haven't tried using a controller, so I can't really say anything about controller support, which the other reviewer had problems with.)\nIf you're a fan of games like Super Meat Boy, you really should check this out.",
